title Caravan reopen -- a reader who says the answer falls short opens the matter again
prompt Take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, Standfast on reds first, deep-read one council-rota doc, condense REMEMBER when a set completes, and send each finished increment as its own signed round.
think Standfast first. Every living row in crux/REDS.md carries its closure note -- %81 closed at the registration gap, %83's booked prevention landed as the living-card ASCII witness, %96 and %97 closed on the one-clock head duty and the ledger scan that learned the prose shape. No open agent-closable red stands, so the constructive queue is honestly open.
think Council rota, lap index 82 mod 27 = 1 -- foundations/README.md, deep-read. Its one line governed this lap: these rest beneath the specifications; the specs say what to build and how, these say what it is for. The rung below asks a reader what they make of an answer; the question this lap had to answer is what the asking is FOR, and the honest answer is that it is for nothing at all unless something follows from it.
think The running thread, read off the newest log's recommend: the suffice rung reads a reader's word saying the answer falls short, publishes it honestly -- and then a supervisor may learn every run that its answer settled nothing and go on answering exactly the same way forever. That is the crux, and it is agent-doable in the arc's own idiom.
think The name wanted care. `amend` was already taken -- it corrects a settlement an operator already read -- as were `recant` and `appraise`. Under the Comlink tendency I took the clearest, warmest, safest word for the act: reopen. Six tree hits, every one HUNK image-witness prose in an unrelated domain, no module of that name.
think The design's real content is not the note; it is who gets to write one. Every rung of this arc reaches outward to be TOLD something -- a quarrel, a standing, a third hand's finding, a reader's verdict -- and the plan has always decided by itself what to do about it. This rung is the first where what the plan is told costs it a look it never chose to take.
think Two notes in the arc are now addressed forward, and naming their difference is what made the rung buildable. `owe` books what the plan itself conceded; `reopen` books what its reader says is still wanting. A plan may keep its own word, concede nothing, owe nothing -- and still be reopened by the person it answered.
think The refusal ladder had to protect the rung below rather than only itself. Booking a matter open against a reader who says it settles would punish a plan for asking, and would teach every supervisor never to ask at all -- undoing suffice in a single lap. So `ReopenSettled` refuses by name, satisfaction costs nothing, and dissatisfaction costs exactly one more look.
think Both marks of the measured lap now weigh, where suffice's marks parted on the weighing itself. So the bare run had to be moved from .unasked to .asks and the judge rewritten to expect weighed=1 under both -- otherwise the new number would have been riding on the old one's difference rather than standing on its own.
obs Six RED paths proven on metal before any GREEN claim, each by disarming one guard and rebuilding: skip the write and the run refuses ReopenMisrecorded; read the reader as never asked, ReopenUnweighed; read their word as settling, ReopenSettled; read a note about some other word, ReopenMismatched; count one short word both ways, ReopenMiscounted. The sixth is the planted control -- write, read-back, and both harness reads disarmed at once -- and the selftest printed GREEN while caravan/.reopens/plan.again did not exist at all. Seeing that is what makes the reading back a check rather than decoration.
obs An honest ratchet, measured rather than recalled, and surfaced rather than fixed unilaterally: each rung of this arc carries a full copy of every check below it, so the modules grow about 500 lines per rung -- heed 7,890 lines, suffice 14,095, reopen 14,609, and 95 percent of a rung's unique lines appear verbatim in the rung above it. The implementations are imported, so this is the accumulated self-test rather than duplicated logic, and the suite already sings every rung. The growth is real and compounding; whether to fold the ladder's checks into one shared harness is a design call worth Keaton's eye rather than an autonomous rewrite of 82 modules.
loom witness=caravan_reopen_witness wall_ms=10300 module_lines=14609 module_bytes=669980 checks=72 red_paths_on_metal=6
loom measure=reopen short_words_read=1 taken_up_closing=0 taken_up_taking_up=1 unheeded_closing=1 unheeded_taking_up=0 note_bytes=4
file caravan/reopen.rye the rung itself -- the enum, the four-byte note, the refusal ladder, the run step, and the folds
file tools/caravan_reopen_witness.rish the witness -- six RED paths on metal, one a planted control that printed GREEN with the note absent
file tools/caravan_suite_witness.rish registers the new rung so it can never run unheard
file caravan/README.md the rung-by-rung record gains its section
file .gitignore the new note dir stays out of the tree
file crux/REMEMBER.md the live edge moves to this rung and the prior one folds down
recommend keep-going the arc now corrects a record, carries the correction, hears the answer, records the disagreement, escorts the word, bounds the objection, stands its standing, tells the raiser, reads their reply, carries a live quarrel past the run that heard it, makes the inheriting run answer for it, lets its holder close it, dates it, reads that age aloud, puts a long-standing one before a third hand, reads back what that hand made of it, makes the plan answer that finding on the record, carries the plan's own concession forward, makes the run that inherits it meet it, makes that meeting say what it found, carries that finding home to the reader who won it, reads what that reader makes of it, and now takes the matter up again when they say it falls short -- so the question above is what the run that inherits a reopened matter actually does with it, since nothing yet asks a later run to look again at what a reader called short, exactly as nothing asked one to meet an inherited debt until the meet rung. Beside it stands the ratchet named in obs: the per-rung check copy, growing 500 lines a lap.
